  "result": "The quiz is written to `quizzes/0002.json`, with its key in `keys/0002.json`. It has six items on O4 (who owns the control flow, and when a fixed workflow is the better choice).\n\nThere was no lesson on O4, so this quiz is ahead of the lessons.\n\nThe items cover these ideas:\n- **Who owns the control flow (q1, q2):** the model chooses the next step in an agent, while code fixes the order in a workflow. A model that runs inside the code's sequence doesn't make the design an agent.\n- **Deciding on a fixed workflow (q3, q5):** choose one when the steps are known in advance and the same every time. Choose an agent when the next step depends on what was just found.\n- **Cost of the choice (q4):** how much extra an agent costs when its flexibility isn't used.\n- **Fixing an agent that's the wrong fit (q6):** a diagnosis of an agent that is costly and unreliable on a task with fixed steps.\n\nThe quiz-reviewer ran two passes. I fixed every finding from both, but I didn't run a third pass on the final wording. Its findings and my changes are in `review-records/0002-quiz.md`.\n\nSend me your answers when you're ready and I'll grade them.",
